From eba39b884504fb0eb6a41610deb1920958b6b91e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Omsi-Hub <lucruigrok@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 19:24:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Skins: a plugin's look for the loading screen, the pause menu
 and the navigator

A folder plugin can bring plugins/<name>/skin.json, chosen with skin=<name> in settings.cfg or
--skin <name>. It gives the theme's colours (omsi_ui::theme's colours are read through
functions now, so a skin can change them), the loading screen's logo, colours and tips, the
pause menu's name, mark and up to six lines of the plugin's own (a click is the new
menu_entry event), and the navigator's and city map's colours over the light and dark
palettes. Read once before the window opens; one that cannot be read is logged and the game
keeps its own look. Documented in docs/PLUGINS.md "Skins".

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WaHFnKQnB1G3cjLxZp4wv4
