+### Skins
+
+A folder plugin can bring a **skin**: another look for the game's own screens - the loading
+screen, the pause menu and its lists, the photo and developer panels and the navigator's map -
+and lines of its own in the pause menu. The skin is `plugins/<name>/skin.json`, beside the
+plugin's `main.lua`, with its pictures in the plugin's folder. It is chosen with `skin=<name>`
+in `settings.cfg` (or `--skin <name>` for one run); it is read once as the game starts, before
+the first loading screen, so it needs no Lua. A skin that cannot be read is said in the log and
+the game keeps its own look.
+
+```json
+{
+  "title": "My Company",
+  "colours": { "accent": "#2A75F7", "accent_hover": "#4C8BF8", "accent_ink": "#FFFFFF", "bg": "#0A142E", "sidebar": "#0D1936" },
+  "loading": {
+    "logo": "skin/wordmark.svg",
+    "background": "#0A142E", "map_name": "#959DB0", "text": "#E8EBF2",
+    "bar": ["#2A75F7", "#5B95F9"], "track": "#1B2747",
+    "tips": ["F9 opens the messages", { "en": "Shift+N shows the board", "nl": "Shift+N toont het bord" }],
+    "tips_only": false
+  },
+  "menu": {
+    "mark": "skin/mark.svg",
+    "entries": [{ "id": "duty", "label": "My duty", "icon": "badge", "after": "resume" }]
+  },
+  "map_dark": { "land": "#0A142E", "route": "#2A75F7" },
+  "map_light": { "route": "#2A75F7" }
+}
+```
+
+Every key is optional:
+
+| Key | What it changes |
+| --- | --- |
+| `title` | the name in the pause menu's sidebar, in place of "openOMSI" |
+| `colours` | the interface's colours by name (`#RRGGBB` or `#RRGGBBAA`): `accent`, `accent_2`, `accent_hover`, `accent_ink`, `danger`, `danger_2`, `ok`, `warn`, `text`, `text_soft`, `text_dim`, `text_faint`, `rail`, `panel`, `field`, `hover`, `selected`, `edge`, `bg`, `sidebar`, `surface`, `surface_2`, `surface_3`, `ink`, `ink_2`, `ink_muted` (as `omsi_ui::theme` has them) |
+| `loading.logo` | the loading screen's logo in place of the wordmark: an SVG, PNG, JPEG, BMP or TGA of the plugin's folder (at most 4 MB), drawn as wide as the wordmark |
+| `loading.background`, `map_name`, `text`, `track` | the loading screen's ground, the map's name and the tip, the percentage, the bar's track |
+| `loading.bar` | the bar's stripes: two colours, or one for a plain bar; the "Tips" heading takes the first |
+| `loading.tips` | up to 40 tips, shown among the game's (`tips_only = true`: in their place); a tip is a text, or a table of texts by language (`en`, `nl`, `de` ...) |
+| `menu.mark` | the square picture beside the name in the pause menu's sidebar |
+| `menu.entries` | up to 6 lines of the plugin's own in the pause menu: `id` (letters, digits, `_` and `-`), `label` (a text or a table by language), `icon` (a Material Symbols name, as `omsi.ui`'s icons), `after` (the id of the game's line it follows - `resume`, `options`, `map`, `save` ...; left out: before "End the session") |
+| `map_dark`, `map_light` | the navigator's and the city map's colours over the dark and the light look: `land`, `grass`, `forest`, `field`, `paved_land`, `sand`, `water`, `road`, `road_edge`, `foot`, `area`, `lane_paint`, `lane_amber`, `roof`, `roof_edge`, `wall_lit`, `wall_dark`, `shadow`, `tree`, `tree_edge`, `rail`, `rail_dash`, `tram`, `route`, `route_edge`, `driven`, `card`, `card_text`, `card_dim`, `label`, `label_halo`, `contour` |
+
+A click on one of the skin's lines closes the menu and is the `menu_entry` event, with the
+line's `id`:
+
+```lua
+omsi.on("menu_entry", function(id)
+  if id == "duty" then show_my_duty() end
+end)
+```
+
